### ====================================================================
### Module 04: Scheduling - EOD Banking Cut-Off & Ledger Reconciliation
### Interactive REST Client Test Scenarios
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@periodDate = 2026-09-23
@discrepancyDate = 2026-09-24

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. System Health & Readiness Check
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthCheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Happy Path Workflow: Balanced EOD Reconciliation
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Seed Balanced Ledger Entries ($15,000.00 credits & debits)
# @name seedBalanced
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/seed HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "{{periodDate}}",
    "scenario": "balanced",
    "amount_cents": 1500000
}

### Step B: Audit Business-Day Gaps
# @name auditGaps
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/gaps HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### Step C: Trigger Manual EOD Cut-off Reconciliation
# @name triggerCutoff
# NOTE: This endpoint dispatches an ASYNCHRONOUS Celery task and returns HTTP 202 Accepted.
# Allow 1-2 seconds for the Celery worker to aggregate balances and commit to PostgreSQL before Step D.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/trigger HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "{{periodDate}}",
    "clearing_variance_cents": 0,
    "force": false
}

### Step D: Inspect Reconciled Report by Period Date
# @name getReport
# Query after the Celery worker completes the reconciliation task dispatched in Step C.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/{{periodDate}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### Step E: List Paginated Reports
# @name listReports
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations?limit=10&offset=0 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Discrepancy Detection Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Seed Ledger Entries for Discrepancy Period
# @name seedDiscrepancy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/seed HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "{{discrepancyDate}}",
    "scenario": "discrepancy",
    "amount_cents": 2500000
}

### Step B: Trigger Reconciliation with $200.00 Clearinghouse Variance
# @name triggerDiscrepancy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/trigger HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "{{discrepancyDate}}",
    "clearing_variance_cents": 20000,
    "force": false
}

### Step C: Inspect Flagged Discrepancy Report
# @name getDiscrepancyReport
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/{{discrepancyDate}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Idempotency Verification Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Re-trigger reconciliation for already-reconciled period date
# @name triggerIdempotency
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/trigger HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "{{periodDate}}",
    "clearing_variance_cents": 0,
    "force": false
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Error Handling & Validation Scenarios
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scenario A: Non-Existent Period Date (Expected: HTTP 404 Not Found)
# @name getNonExistent
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/1999-01-01 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### Scenario B: Invalid Period Date Format (Expected: HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity)
# @name invalidDateValidation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/trigger HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "period_date": "not-a-valid-date",
    "clearing_variance_cents": 0
}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Historical Gap Audit & On-Demand Backfill Workflow
### --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Step A: Audit Missing Business-Day Gaps
# @name auditGaps
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/gaps HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### Step B: Trigger On-Demand Gap Backfill (Default Scan)
# @name triggerBackfillDefault
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/backfill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### Step C: Trigger On-Demand Gap Backfill (Custom Date Range)
# @name triggerBackfillRange
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reconciliations/backfill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "start_date": "2026-09-01",
    "end_date": "2026-09-22"
}

